AGPL, not GPL, is deliberate. Marum is offered as a hosted service, and section
13 of the AGPL is what makes that honest: anyone who runs a modified Marum over
a network must offer its source to the people using it. Plain GPLv3 does not
reach network use, which is the only distribution model this project has.
